ressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UEDA HIDEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HONDA, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATSUMA, KEITA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NARUSE, TSUTOMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OMOTE, TAKUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UEDA, HIDEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A polyester monofilament of the core-sheath structure for screen gauze, characterized in that the sheath is made of a polyester which has a degree of coloration through heating at 175  DEG C for 1 hour (APHA) of 30 or lower and is obtained through copolymerization with a polyalkylene oxide having a number-average molecular weight of 300 to 4,000 used in an amount of 2 to 10 wt.% based on the polyester, and in which the mechanical loss tangent (tan delta ) thereof measured at a frequency of 110 Hz has a peak temperature (Tmax) which is 97 to 120  DEG C and is lower by at least 10  DEG C than that of the core, and that the core/sheath areal ratio is 60/40 to 90/10. The monofilament is completely free from scum generation during weaving, has satisfactory suitability for gauze formation, and gives a high-mesh screen gauze excellent in dimensional stability and adhesion to photosensitive resins.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un monofilament de polyester à structure à âme gainée pour treillis, caractérisé en ce que la gaine est faite d'un polyester dont le degré de coloration suite à un chauffage à 175  DEG C pendant une heure (APHA) est de 30 ou moins et qui est obtenu par copolymérisation avec un oxyde de polyakylène présentant un poids moléculaire moyen en nombre de 200 à 4000 utilisé à raison de 2 à 10 % en poids du polyester. Dans ce monofilament de polyester, la tangente de perte mécanique (tan delta ), mesurée à une fréquence de 110 Hz, a une température maxi (Tmax) comprise entre 97 et 120  DEG C, ce qui est inférieur d'au moins 10  DEG C à celle de l'âme, le rapport de surface âme/gaine se situant entre 60/40 et 90/10. Le monofilament ne libère aucune écume pendant le tissage, convient pour la fabrication de treillis et permet d'obtenir un treillis à mailles serrées présentant d'excellentes caractéristiques en termes de stabilité dimensionnelle et d'adhérence à des résines photosensibles.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>